# Berserk: "Target creature" is any creature, and the delayed trigger destroys it if "it attacked this turn" whoever
# controls it. Bot2's Embereth Shieldbreaker attacks on turn 4 and Bot1, who has an instant-speed Berserk and a Forest,
# casts it on the attacker in the declare attackers step: it hits for 4 (2 + 2, trample) and is destroyed at the end
# step, though Bot1 does not control it.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Berserk
Forest x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Embereth Shieldbreaker
Mountain x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Embereth Shieldbreaker.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Attack(Embereth Shieldbreaker > Bot1)
Bot1.Hand.Berserk.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Embereth Shieldbreaker)
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield.Embereth Shieldbreaker.Power = 4
[T5 Bot1.Upkeep]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 16
Bot2.Graveyard = Embereth Shieldbreaker
Bot2.Battlefield = Mountain; Mox Ruby
Bot1.Graveyard = Berserk
